25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It appears we have a surplus of applicants for coding roles, but a worrying void in phenotyping technicians. The glasshouse crew, however, remains strong.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Shipping costs are rising while per-diems are frozen, though the ministry is still subsidizing glasshouse space. Also, repository deposits are now clearing very quickly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Computing is currently free under the new agreement, but animal-unit rates have spiked. The animal facility is well-staffed, but the glasshouses are completely full.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Shared spectroscopy was down for eleven weeks due to a lapsed contract. Furthermore, projects relying on live breeding colonies are far more prone to delays.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Catalogue-style projects have shown the most enduring utility. Conversely, field sites are currently highly unstable due to flooding and fire.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, if the glasshouses are booked solid, we must be cautious about any proposal requiring significant greenhouse space.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, that is a good point. Though the subsidy helps, the lack of physical space is a different matter.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, exactly. I'm also worried about the animal costs Benjamin mentioned.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, if field sites are failing, we should avoid any project that depends on outdoor collection this year.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The data suggests indoor or simulation-based work is currently more reliable.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the lack of spectroscopy engineers is also a red flag for high-end lab work.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, since computing is free, perhaps a project with a heavy simulation component would be the most cost-effective?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that sounds like a great idea! It avoids the animal costs and the glasshouse crowds.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, I concur. Logic suggests we pivot toward computation to avoid the biological and mechanical bottlenecks.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, the loss of phenotyping technicians further supports moving away from complex biological sampling.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
