50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Microbiome Atlas, B: Plant Drought Signaling, C: Protein Folding Dynamics, and D: Regeneration in Amphibians. I lean toward C.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Midori,,"C seems very balanced. It uses simulation, which is currently free, and avoids the glasshouse shortage.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I like C too! It doesn't need the animal facility or the crowded greenhouses.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,C is the most rational choice. It avoids the breeding colony risks and the field site instability Toshio found.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A depends on field sites, B on glasshouses, and D on breeding colonies. C is the only one that aligns with the current infrastructure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, do you think the spectroscopy needs for C will be a problem given the engineer shortage?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, C combines spectroscopy with simulation. If the simulation is the core, the lab delays might be manageable.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Plus, the computing agreement makes the simulation part very easy to fund!","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Servas, the risk is lower than the total failure of a field site or a full glasshouse.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree. C is the most stable path to a successful closeout.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,I am satisfied. C avoids the most critical bottlenecks.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Midori,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Kenji,,C is my choice!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I concur. C it is.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
